<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-ph" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/rotted-eave.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/rotted-eave-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/rotted-eave.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/free-tools/">Free tools</a></li><li aria-current="page">RCV / ACV &amp; Holdback Calculator</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Free calculator</p><h1>RCV / ACV &amp; Holdback Calculator for Property Claims</h1><p class="lede">Most replacement-cost policies pay in two steps: actual cash value first, then the withheld depreciation once repairs are done. This RCV ACV calculator shows both numbers item by item.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="dep">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>RCV / ACV &amp; holdback calculator</span><i>Add a row for each item</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div class="table-wrap items-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Replacement cost ($)</th><th>Age (yrs)</th><th>Life (yrs)</th><th>ACV</th><th><span class="sr-only">Remove</span></th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><input name="item" value="Asphalt shingle roof" aria-label="Item"></td><td><input name="rcv" inputmode="decimal" value="16400" aria-label="Replacement cost"></td><td><input name="age" inputmode="decimal" value="11" aria-label="Age in years"></td><td><input name="life" inputmode="decimal" value="25" aria-label="Expected life in years"></td><td class="mono" data-o="row">$0</td><td><button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove row">×</button></td></tr><tr><td><input name="item" value="Steel siding — two elevations" aria-label="Item"></td><td><input name="rcv" inputmode="decimal" value="7300" aria-label="Replacement cost"></td><td><input name="age" inputmode="decimal" value="18" aria-label="Age in years"></td><td><input name="life" inputmode="decimal" value="40" aria-label="Expected life in years"></td><td class="mono" data-o="row">$0</td><td><button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove row">×</button></td></tr><tr><td><input name="item" value="Gutters &amp; downspouts" aria-label="Item"></td><td><input name="rcv" inputmode="decimal" value="1650" aria-label="Replacement cost"></td><td><input name="age" inputmode="decimal" value="11" aria-label="Age in years"></td><td><input name="life" inputmode="decimal" value="20" aria-label="Expected life in years"></td><td class="mono" data-o="row">$0</td><td><button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove row">×</button></td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-add data-run>+ Add item</button></div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="d-ded">Deductible ($)</label><input id="d-ded" name="deduct" inputmode="decimal" value="2500"></div>
        <div><label for="d-cap">Depreciation cap</label><select id="d-cap" name="cap"><option value="50">50%</option><option value="70">70%</option><option value="80" selected>80%</option><option value="90">90%</option></select><span class="hint">Many estimates cap depreciation on an item. Check yours.</span></div>
      </div>
      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nonrec"> My policy (or this item) pays actual cash value only</label>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out wide-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="out-big"><small>First payment (ACV − deductible)</small><b data-o="first">$0</b></div>
      <div class="out-big"><small>Held back until repairs</small><b data-o="held">$0</b></div>
      <div class="out-big"><small>Total if fully recovered</small><b data-o="total">$0</b></div>
      <div class="out-rows span-all">
        <div><span>Replacement cost value (RCV)</span><b data-o="rcv">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Total depreciation</span><b data-o="dep">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Depreciation as share of RCV</span><b data-o="deppct">0%</b></div>
        <div><span>Actual cash value (ACV)</span><b data-o="acv">$0</b></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why the first check looks low</h2>
<p>On a replacement cost policy, the insurer usually pays <strong>actual cash value</strong> first: replacement cost minus depreciation, minus your deductible. The depreciation is held back until you repair or replace, subject to the policy’s conditions and time limits. That holdback can be a large share of a roof or siding claim.</p>
<h2>How this RCV ACV calculator estimates depreciation</h2>
<p>Each row uses straight-line depreciation: age ÷ expected life × replacement cost, limited by the cap you choose. Real estimates may depreciate labor differently, use condition adjustments or apply no depreciation to some items. Treat the result as a way to check whether the carrier’s depreciation looks reasonable, not as the final figure.</p>
<h2>Questions worth asking about depreciation</h2>
<ul>
<li>Is depreciation applied to labor as well as materials, and does your policy allow it?</li>
<li>Does the life used for a 30-year architectural shingle match the product?</li>
<li>Is the age based on records, or an adjuster’s guess?</li>
<li>Does the policy require repairs within a set period to recover the holdback?</li>
</ul>
<p>Tick “actual cash value only” for older roofs or items your policy settles on ACV. Example values are illustrative.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is recoverable depreciation?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It is the part of the replacement cost withheld from the first payment that the insurer pays after repairs are completed, if the policy provides replacement cost coverage.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can depreciation be disputed in appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often yes, as part of the amount of loss, depending on the policy wording. Age, condition and expected life are common disagreement points.</p></div></details><details><summary>Why is there a depreciation cap?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many estimates limit how much an item can be depreciated so it never drops to zero. The right cap depends on the estimate and the policy.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/free-tools/roof-area-pitch-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Roof Area &amp; Pitch Calculator</span><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/free-tools/percentage-deductible-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Percentage De